      "updated": 1793966400000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": true,
      "customData": {
        "title": "The app calls one agent",
        "description": "A signed-in user's browser gets a Foundry token through the web app's single-page sign-in registration. The Azure Container Apps web app's proxy forwards only that token and the question to the Foundry hosted agent's Responses endpoint, and Foundry keeps each user's conversations private. The agent's project toolbox queries the bound ontology through Fabric IQ as that user and retrieves document evidence from the Foundry IQ knowledge base with the project's managed identity, so documents are not trimmed per user. The app holds no credential or shared token, and deployment consent is a separate boundary. Prove the fresh challenge, live facts, a cited document and second-user denial and isolation separately; other users need an operator-granted role. Cold sessions and live ontology queries can take a minute.",
        "role": "page"
      },
      "index": "a0"
    },
